{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Streaming devices, a voice assistant, a reader and a home camera do not solve the computer connection needs reflected in my purchases.",
    "The HDMI cable is close to my practical accessory interests, but buying a DVI cable does not mean I currently need a different display connection.",
    "My earlier headset purchase gives me no current reason to buy speakers or another pair of earphones, and I have no specific storage need for the memory card."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations treat interest in computer accessories as interest in electronics generally.",
    "Buying an Anker USB expansion card seems to have been stretched into interest in an Anker speaker, even though they serve different purposes."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My purchases mostly address specific tasks: adding ports, connecting to a network, connecting a display or mounting a tablet. The particular task matters more to me than a broad resemblance between devices.",
    "My purchases are widely spaced, and owning an accessory does not mean I need to replace it or add another one now.",
    "Connection types and compatibility matter: a cable or adapter is useful only when it fits the equipment and connection I actually need."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized a broad interest in electronics but missed my occasional, specific need for practical connections and accessories."
}"}
